<title>USA: RESEARCH ALERT-InterCel, Western Wireless.</title>
<headline>RESEARCH ALERT-InterCel, Western Wireless.</headline>
<text>
<p>-- Oppenheimer &amp; Co Inc said on Tuesday it began coverage of two wireless telecommunications companies, InterCel Inc and Western Wireless Corp, both with an outperform rating.</p>
<p>-- Analyst Thomas Lee gave InterCel a 12-month target price of $30, citing its densely populated urban markets, first to market timing advantage, experienced management and strategic alliances.</p>
<p>-- InterCel closed at 21 on Monday.</p>
<p>-- Lee gave Western Wireless a 12-month target of $27, citing its continguous rural cellular and urban PCS licenses. He also said its cellular assets are trading at 8.8 times 1997 estimated EBITDA.</p>
<p>-- Western Wireless shares closed at $17.</p>
</text>
